<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <PackageId>BulletMLLib</PackageId>
    <Version>5.1.0</Version>
    <Title>BulletMLLib</Title>
    <Authors>dmanning23</Authors>
    <description>Library for parsing BulletML xml files. Used for scripting bullet patterns in shmup games.</description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>monogame</PackageTags>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
5.1.1

Load errors now say where the problem is. ParseXML throws a BulletMLException whose message names the file, the problem, and the line and column, for example:
Error reading "Content/boss.xml": changeSpeed requires a term child (line 12, column 4)
- BulletMLException has FileName, LineNumber and LinePosition properties. It derives from Exception, and its InnerException is still InvalidDataException (or XmlException for malformed XML), so 5.1 catch code keeps working.
- A misspelled element name is reported as an unknown element with its location, instead of an ArgumentException.
- CDATA sections are read as text.
- A ref whose label points at nothing throws InvalidDataException with its location, instead of NullReferenceException.
- An invalid type on the root bulletml element is reported like any other invalid type.

Upgrading from 5.0? 5.1.0 made pattern validation much stricter. See the full release notes before upgrading.

Full release notes: https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MonoGame.Framework.DesktopGL" Version="3.8.*">
      <PrivateAssets>All</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Vector2Extensions" Version="5.*"/>
    <PackageReference Include="Equationator" Version="5.*"/>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>